.TH LARZ-CODE 1 "2026" "LarzOS" "LarzOS Manual"
.SH NAME
larz-code \- Claude Code, Anthropic's terminal coding agent, on LarzOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B larz code
[\fICLAUDE-CODE-ARGS\fR]
.br
.B larz-code
[\fICLAUDE-CODE-ARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts Claude Code in the current directory. Claude Code is Anthropic's
agentic coding tool: it reads and edits files, runs commands, and works
through multi\-step tasks from a natural\-language prompt.
.PP
It is preinstalled on LarzOS (the \fBlarz-claude-code\fR package). If the
\fBclaude\fR command is missing when you run \fBlarz code\fR, it is fetched
via npm automatically.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Auth is yours, not the OS's. On the first run Claude Code walks you through
signing in with your Anthropic account. Alternatively set an API key:
.PP
.RS
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk\-ant\-...
.RE
.PP
Add that line to \fI~/.larzsh/env\fR to make it persist.
.SH LARZSCRIPT IS THE DEFAULT
LarzOS tells Claude Code that Larzscript is the system's default coding
language. \fI/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md\fR is a managed\-policy memory file \-
Claude Code loads it on every session in every repository and it cannot be
excluded by user settings. \fBlarz-code\fR additionally passes a matching
\fB--append-system-prompt\fR line; set \fBLARZOS_NO_SYSPROMPT=1\fR to skip it.
.SH GATEWAY ROUTING
\fI/etc/larzos/claude-code.toml\fR may name a \fBbase_url\fR and
\fBauth_token\fR. When both are set, \fBlarz-code\fR exports
\fBANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\fR and \fBANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN\fR so Claude Code talks
to that endpoint instead of api.anthropic.com \- use this to route through
the LarzOS Gateway.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/larzos/claude-code.toml
Optional gateway routing config.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR larz (1),
.BR larz-ai (8)
